  "texts": {
    "g_phrase": "Spell this whole phrase.",
    "p_bossy-r": "Two new ideas today, and both are about bossy r. First: when R comes after the letter A, or the letter O, it changes the sound. A, R says [[ɑɹ|ar]], like star. O, R says [[ɔɹ|or]], like corn. Second: E, R, and I, R, and U, R all say the same sound, [[ɝ|er]], like her, bird, and fur. You have to remember which one each word uses.",
    "p_ck-sh": "Two new ideas today. First: at the end of a short word, after a short vowel, the k sound is spelled c, k, like sock and duck. Second: some letters team up to make one new sound. S, H says [[ʃ|sh]], like fish. C, H says [[tʃ|ch]], like chin. And T, H says [[θ|th]], like bath.",
    "p_double": "Two new ideas today. First: at the end of a short word, right after a short vowel, f, l, s, and z are doubled, like puff, shell, dress, and buzz. Second: heart words. Most of a heart word follows the rules, but one part is tricky, so we learn that part by heart, like the a, i in said.",
    "p_ng-tch": "Two new ideas today. First: glued sounds. N and g glue together, like ring and song. N and k glue together, like pink and trunk. Second: right after a short vowel, the [[tʃ|ch]] sound is spelled t, c, h, like match. And the [[dʒ|j]] sound is spelled d, g, e, like badge.",
    "p_review-1": "Review time! This wing mixes everything from levels one, two, and three: c, k at the end, the letter teams s, h, and c, h, and t, h, bossy r, double letters, and heart words. Show what you know!",
    "p_silent-e": "Two new ideas today. First: silent e. An e at the end of a word is silent, but it makes the vowel say its name. Kit becomes kite. Second: soft c and soft g. When c comes before e, i, or y, it says [[s|s]], like city. When g comes before e, i, or y, it often says [[dʒ|j]], like gem.",
    "p_teams": "Two new ideas today, and both are vowel teams: two letters that make one long sound. First: long a and long e. A, I goes in the middle, like rain, and A, Y goes at the end, like play. Long e is E, E or E, A, like tree and leaf. Second: long o and long i. O, A goes in the middle, like boat, and O, W goes at the end, like snow. Long i can be I, G, H, like light, or I, E, like pie.",
